// Dart program to implement the insertion sort algorithm

void insertionSort(List<int> arr) {
  int n = arr.length;
  for (int I = 1; I < n; ++i) {
    int key = arr[i];
    int j = I - 1;

    /* Move elements of arr[0..i-1], that are
       greater than key, to one position ahead
       of their current position */
    while (j >= 0 && arr[j] > key) {
      arr[j + 1] = arr[j];
      j = j - 1;
    }
    arr[j + 1] = key; // Insert the key element in its correct position
  }
}

// Driver code to test the insertion sort function
void main() {
  List<int> arr = [12, 11, 13, 5, 6];
  print("Original array: $arr");

  insertionSort(arr);

  print("Sorted array: $arr");
}
```

Explanation:

In this program, we have defined a function called `insertionSort` that accepts an unsorted list of integers as input. We start by initializing the `n` variable to the length of the input list. We choose the first element `arr[0]` as the sorted element and then insert each remaining element of the input list one by one into the sorted sequence.

For each iteration of the `for` loop, we choose the key element `arr[i]` and start moving the elements of the sorted sequence that are greater than the key element one position ahead to create space for the key element. Finally, we insert the key element at its correct position based on the comparison with the elements of the sorted sequence.

The program also includes a `main` function that tests the `insertionSort` function using a sample input list `[12, 11, 13, 5, 6]`. The output of the program is the sorted list `[5, 6, 11, 12, 13]`.

